/ A json array parses into a plang list (ruling 5), through the json type's own parse.
/ The read goes first (decision 401), then `%l% is list` is true. Today's parse yields
/ a C# JsonElement, so `is list` reads false even after a successful index read.
ArrayIsAList
- read list.json, write to %l%
- assert.equals(Expected=1, Actual=%l[0]%, Message="the first read goes through the json type")
- condition.if(Left=%l%, Operator="is", Right="list") { variable.set(Name=%isList%, Value=true) }
- assert.equals(Expected=true, Actual=%isList%, Message="after the read, %l% is a plang list")
